| Failures                 | 0                    | 0                    | 0              |
+--------------------------+----------------------+----------------------+----------------+

Interpretation
  Fix114 is an incremental extension of Fix61 and therefore inherits the
  accepted SceneLM/SceneProof pipeline: independent full SO(3), guarded local
  optimization, collision partial commit, component certificates, rollback,
  and the established pose/runtime result. It adds generic true-mesh vertical
  first-contact support repair with per-object transactional acceptance.

Paper positioning
  Main method / final visual output: Fix114.
  Required ablation / quantitative anchor: Fix61 (Fix114 without the final
  true-mesh vertical-support repair).
  Claim aggregate physical non-inferiority and collision improvement. Do not
  claim every family improves: the legacy OBB support proxy drops by 0.443 pp.
  Report this openly and explain that Fix114 optimizes certified true-mesh
  contact while the legacy support family remains a proxy metric.

